hadiths[14]{hadithnumber,text}:
"969","1003 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from Hammam ibn Munabbih, who said: This is what Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to us, from Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A vow brings the son of Adam nothing I had not decreed for him; rather the vow meets what I had decreed for him. I extract thereby from the miser; he gives Me thereby what he would not have given Me before."
"970","1004 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Ismail, meaning Ibn Ulayyah, narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Thaqif were allies of Banu Uqayl, and Thaqif captured two men of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) captured a man of Banu Uqayl and seized with him al-Adba'. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him while he was in bonds, and he said: O Muhammad! O Muhammad! So he came to him and said: What is your concern? He said: Why did you seize me, and why did you seize the vanguard of the pilgrims? He said, magnifying that. He said: I seized you for the crime of your allies, Thaqif. Then he turned away from him, and he called out to him: O Muhammad! O Muhammad! And the Messenger of Allah was merciful and gentle, so he returned to him and said: What is your concern? He said: I am a Muslim. He said: Had you said it while you controlled your own affair, you would have prospered fully. Then he turned away from him, and he called out to him: O Muhammad! O Muhammad! So he came to him and said: What is your concern? He said: I am hungry, so feed me, and thirsty, so give me drink. He said: This is your need. He said: So he was ransomed in exchange for the two men. And a woman of the Ansar was captured, and al-Adba' was seized. The woman was in bonds, and the people used to graze their livestock in front of their houses. One night she slipped out of her bonds and came to the camels; whenever she approached a camel it growled, so she left it, until she reached al-Adba', which did not growl. It was a trained she-camel, so she mounted its rump, then urged it on and it set off. They were alerted about her, pursued her, but she eluded them. He said: And she had vowed that if Allah saved her, she would slaughter it. When she reached Madinah, the people saw it and said: Al-Adba', the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: She vowed that if Allah saved her, she would slaughter it. So they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and he said: Glory be to Allah! What an evil reward she gave her: that since Allah saved her, she would slaughter it? There is no fulfillment in disobedience of Allah, nor in what the servant does not own."
"971","1005 - Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Uqbah narrated to me, he said: Ubaydullah informed us. And Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Warraq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Talhah ibn Abd al-Malik, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever vows to obey Allah, let him obey Him; and whoever vows to disobey Him, let him not disobey Him."
"972","1006 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, he said: Khattab narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Karim narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Vows are of two kinds: what is for Allah, its expiation is fulfillment; and what is for Satan, there is no fulfillment in it, and upon him is the expiation of an oath."
"973","1007 - Hammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Anbasah al-Warraq narrated to us, he said: Dawud narrated to us, from Hammam, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from Uqbah ibn Amir, may Allah be pleased with him, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about his sister, who vowed to walk to the Ka'bah, and he said: Allah is in no need of your sister's vow; let her ride and offer a sacrificial animal. 1008 - And Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated it from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, without mentioning: let her offer a sacrificial animal."
"974","1009 - Abu Ja'far al-Darimi narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Yahya, meaning Ibn Ayyub, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from Uqbah ibn Amir, may Allah be pleased with him, that his sister vowed to walk to the House, so he sought a ruling for her from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Command her to ride. And Abu al-Khayr used to keep close to Uqbah."
"975","1010 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to me, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: While the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was present, there was a man standing in the sun. He asked about him, and they said: This is Abu Isra'il; he vowed to stand and not sit, not seek shade, not speak, and to fast. He said: Command him to speak, seek shade, sit, and complete his fast."
"976","1011 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Humayd informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man being supported between his two sons, and said: What is this? They said: He vowed to walk to the House. He said: Allah is in no need of this one's tormenting himself. So he ordered him to ride."
"977","1012 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Ibn Abbas, from Sa'd, that he said: My mother died with a vow upon her, so I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he commanded me to fulfill it on her behalf."
"978","1013 - Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi and Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, I vowed in the Days of Ignorance to spend a night in retreat in the Sacred Mosque. He said to him: Fulfill your vow."
"979","1014 - Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Hakam, Muslim al-Batin, and Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, Mujahid, and Ata, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my sister died with two consecutive months of fasting upon her. He said: If your sister owed a debt, would you pay it? She said: Yes. He said: Then the right of Allah is more deserving."
"980","1015 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ja'far, that Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to him, from Urwah, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies with fasting upon him, his guardian fasts on his behalf."
"981","1016 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa, meaning Ibn Yunus, informed us, from Shu'bah, from Ja'far ibn Iyas, who said: I heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr narrating from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My sister vowed to perform pilgrimage, and she died. He said: If she owed a debt, would you pay it? He said: Yes. He said: Then pay Allah, for He is most deserving of fulfillment."
"982","1017 - al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Habib al-Mu'allim, from Ata, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man vowed to pray in Bayt al-Maqdis, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Pray here, meaning in the Sacred Mosque. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I vowed to pray in Bayt al-Maqdis. He said: Pray here."
